QR-Based Attendance System

About the Project
The QR-Based Attendance System is a web application that helps teachers record and manage student attendance using QR codes. Students can scan a QR code to mark their attendance, making the process easier and faster.

Features
- Student, teacher, and admin login
- Student and teacher registration
- QR code generation for attendance sessions
- QR code scanning to mark attendance
- Student attendance history
- Teacher attendance management
- Subject management
- Database storage using MongoDB

Technologies Used

Frontend
- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript

Backend
- Node.js
- Express.js

Database
- MongoDB Atlas

Other Tools
- Git and GitHub
- Render for deployment
- QR code generation and scanning libraries

